+class BaseMove(NamedTuple):
+    """Who can act on a bundle the fold held because the base moved under the line (#749,
+    :func:`_held_by_move`; :func:`fold`'s ``moved``), each list in merge order. Exactly one
+    of ``stranded`` and ``past`` is not empty, and each bundle in it is one the move puts
+    in the held branch's clash — trial-checked, never read off the files:
+
+    * ``stranded``: bundles on the line whose own change does not merge cleanly onto the
+      base the held branch holds, nor onto ``base`` now. ``base`` moved since their branches
+      were cut, and the held branch carries that move: their branches are to be rebuilt on
+      the new ``base``. The held bundle's change is not what clashes with them there.
+    * ``past``: bundles on the line whose own change does not merge cleanly onto the base
+      the held branch holds, but does onto ``base`` now. ``base`` has moved on since the
+      held branch was built: the held branch is to be updated from ``base``.
+    * ``own``: with ``stranded``, the bundles on the line the held branch's own change also
+      conflicts with (a stranded one among them, maybe): the ordinary overlap of #674 /
